<%# Honest fallback rendered when the interactive RSC client-reference manifests are
    missing or unreachable at runtime. Keeps the demo shell intact and replaces the
    interactive island with a clear, on-brand notice so a visitor never sees a blank
    or broken surface. %>
<%= render "hello_server/styles" %>

<div class="ror-demo-page">
  <%= render "hello_server/hero" %>

  <section class="notice" data-rsc-fallback>
    <p class="badge">RSC manifests unavailable</p>
    <h2>The interactive island is not live on this build</h2>
    <p>
      The async server component above renders fine on the server, but its interactive
      client island (the <code>LikeButton</code>) is intentionally not wired up here. The
      React Server Components client/server manifests that the client-reference path needs
      at runtime were not available to this request, so rather than ship a blank or broken
      widget we are showing this honest note instead.
    </p>
    <p>
      This fallback is a deployment/runtime guard, not the expected public-demo path.
      Rebuild the Rspack assets, verify both RSC manifests are served, and read the current
      RSC status in
      <a href="<%= github_source_url("SPIKE.md") %>" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">SPIKE.md</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <%= render "hello_server/cards" %>
</div>
